@startuml

'skinparam ClassBorderColor #F1C40F
skinparam ClassBorderColor #D4AC0D
skinparam stereotypeABorderColor #A9DCDF
skinparam stereotypeIBorderColor #B4A7E5
skinparam stereotypeCBorderColor #ADD1B2
skinparam stereotypeEBorderColor #EB93DF
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam StateBorderColor #D4AC0D
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #D4AC0D

' Red
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<red>> #FDEDEC
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<red>> #E74C3C
hide <<red>> stereotype
' Purple
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<purple>> #F4ECF7
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<purple>> #8E44AD
hide <<purple>> stereotype
' blue
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<blue>> #EBF5FB
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<blue>> #3498DB
hide <<blue>> stereotype
' Green
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<green>> #EAFAF1
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<green>> #2ECC71
hide <<green>> stereotype

' Orange
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<orange>> #FDF2E9
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<orange>> #E67E22
hide <<orange>> stereotype

' Grey
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<grey>> #EAECEE
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<grey>> #2C3E50
hide <<grey>> stereotype

actor "Ticketing Application" as app #gold
participant "Calypso\nCard API" as capi #pink
participant "Calypso Card\nReader" as cardReader #lightBlue
boundary "selected\n**Card**" as card #lightBlue

activate app #gold
activate card #lightBlue

note over app
    The command exchange duration bounds have been set in the security settings,
    per card profile, for the session opening, the session closing and the SV commands.
    A bound is exceeded when the relevant command exchange alone lasts longer than it.
end note

app->app: **start** a card transaction:\n\t- secured with a **symmetric** crypto module\n\t- in **regular** mode, with its security settings

== Bound exceeded inside a secure session ==

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card transaction:\n\t- open secure session (DEBIT access level)\n\t- read environment file
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->capi: <font color=red>**process**</font> commands
activate capi  #pink

capi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #1**</font>\ntransmit card request\n\t- APDU list
activate cardReader #lightBlue

cardReader->card: open secure session (card debit key,\n\tSFI environment to read)
card-->cardReader: [card challenge, environment data]

note over cardReader
    The exchange lasted longer than the bound set for the session opening:
    a relay attack or a card emulation is suspected.
end note

cardReader--[#0000FF]>capi: [response & effective duration]

capi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #2**</font>\ntransmit card request\n\t- APDU list
cardReader->card: abort secure session
card-->cardReader: ack
deactivate cardReader

capi-->app: <font color=red>**error**</font>: duration bound exceeded
deactivate capi

note over app
    The open secure session is automatically cancelled before the error is raised:
    the card keeps no trace of the interrupted transaction.
end note

== Bound exceeded outside a secure session ==

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card transaction:\n\t- SV Get for Debit
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->capi: <font color=red>**process**</font> commands
activate capi  #pink

capi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #3**</font>\ntransmit card request\n\t- APDU list
activate cardReader #lightBlue

cardReader->card: SV Get (for Debit)
card-->cardReader: [SV Debit record, SV Card challenge]

note over cardReader
    The exchange lasted longer than the bound set for the SV commands.
end note

cardReader--[#0000FF]>capi: [response & effective duration]
deactivate cardReader

capi-->app: <font color=red>**error**</font>: duration bound exceeded
deactivate capi

note over app
    No secure session is open: only the error is raised.
    The ticketing layer decides what to do, according to its own context.
end note

@enduml
